IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mc15-nouns`
IMPORT `mc15-ch49-59`

-- Tests for chapters 49 to 59.  Every expected value was written from the text before the file
-- was run; unit ids (49.1, 52.3 ...) are those of the coverage table in NOTES.md.
-- Exception: the assertions marked `-- RECONCILED` were re-derived after a first run, each from the text and the rule, and each comment quotes the original:
-- in the first pass those that expected a no where the text does not say no in its own words, and in the second pass (2026-10-30) those that expected "not covered"
-- where the text's own "if", "while", "until", "unless" or "except" makes the no (NOTES.md, "Where the text says no, and where it does not").

§ `Tests -- chapters 49 to 59`

§§ `Chapter 49 -- hostages and charters`

-- Arguments are delivered to the King by Englishmen, they are hostages or charters, delivered as sureties of the peace or of faithful service.
#ASSERT `ch 49 -- the hostages and charters are to be restored` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS Obliged
#ASSERT `ch 49 -- the hostages and charters are to be restored` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 49 -- the hostages and charters are to be restored` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 49 -- the hostages and charters are to be restored` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`
-- expect: MUST `restore the hostages and charters delivered to him by Englishmen as sureties of the peace or of faithful service`
#TRACE `ch 49 -- we will immediately restore all hostages and charters delivered to us by Englishmen` TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 49 -- we will immediately restore all hostages and charters delivered to us by Englishmen` TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `restore the hostages and charters delivered to him by Englishmen as sureties of the peace or of faithful service` AT 6
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 49 -- we will immediately restore all hostages and charters delivered to us by Englishmen` FALSE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100

§§ `Chapter 50 -- the relations of Gerard de Athyes`

-- 50.1 and 50.2: every person the text names, and the brothers, the nephew and the whole brood it adds, is to be removed and may have no bailiwick in future.
#ASSERT `ch 50 -- the person is to be removed from his bailiwick` `Engelard de Cygony` EQUALS Obliged
#ASSERT `ch 50 -- the person may have a bailiwick in England in future` `Engelard de Cygony` EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 50 -- the person is to be removed from his bailiwick` `Peter` EQUALS Obliged
#ASSERT `ch 50 -- the person may have a bailiwick in England in future` `Peter` EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 50 -- the person is to be removed from his bailiwick` `Gyon` EQUALS Obliged
#ASSERT `ch 50 -- the person may have a bailiwick in England in future` `Gyon` EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 50 -- the person is to be removed from his bailiwick` `Andrew of the Chancery` EQUALS Obliged
#ASSERT `ch 50 -- the person may have a bailiwick in England in future` `Andrew of the Chancery` EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 50 -- the person is to be removed from his bailiwick` `Gyon de Cygony` EQUALS Obliged
#ASSERT `ch 50 -- the person may have a bailiwick in England in future` `Gyon de Cygony` EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 50 -- the person is to be removed from his bailiwick` `Geoffrey de Martyn` EQUALS Obliged
#ASSERT `ch 50 -- the person may have a bailiwick in England in future` `Geoffrey de Martyn` EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 50 -- the person is to be removed from his bailiwick` `a brother of Geoffrey de Martyn` EQUALS Obliged
#ASSERT `ch 50 -- the person may have a bailiwick in England in future` `a brother of Geoffrey de Martyn` EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 50 -- the person is to be removed from his bailiwick` `Philip Mark` EQUALS Obliged
#ASSERT `ch 50 -- the person may have a bailiwick in England in future` `Philip Mark` EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 50 -- the person is to be removed from his bailiwick` `a brother of Philip Mark` EQUALS Obliged
#ASSERT `ch 50 -- the person may have a bailiwick in England in future` `a brother of Philip Mark` EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 50 -- the person is to be removed from his bailiwick` `Geoffrey, nephew of Philip Mark` EQUALS Obliged
#ASSERT `ch 50 -- the person may have a bailiwick in England in future` `Geoffrey, nephew of Philip Mark` EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 50 -- the person is to be removed from his bailiwick` `another of the whole brood of the same` EQUALS Obliged
#ASSERT `ch 50 -- the person may have a bailiwick in England in future` `another of the whole brood of the same` EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 50 -- the person is to be removed from his bailiwick` `someone not named in the chapter` EQUALS `Obligation not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 50 -- the person may have a bailiwick in England in future` `someone not named in the chapter` EQUALS `Bar not covered`
-- expect: MUST `remove from their bailiwicks the relations of Gerard de Athyes named in chapter 50`
#TRACE `ch 50 -- we will entirely remove from their bailiwicks the relations of Gerard de Athyes` `Peter` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 50 -- we will entirely remove from their bailiwicks the relations of Gerard de Athyes` `Peter` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `remove from their bailiwicks the relations of Gerard de Athyes named in chapter 50` AT 6
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 50 -- we will entirely remove from their bailiwicks the relations of Gerard de Athyes` `someone not named in the chapter` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100

§§ `Chapter 51 -- foreign-born soldiers`

