§§ `Chapter 52 -- lands taken without judgment, and the respite`

-- 52.1: arguments are dispossessed or removed by the King from lands, castles, franchises or right, without the legal judgment of his peers.
#ASSERT `ch 52 -- the lands, castles, franchises or right are to be restored` TRUE TRUE EQUALS Obliged
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30: was "#ASSERT `ch 52 -- the lands, castles, franchises or right are to be restored` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`"; now the text's no, because "If any one has been dispossessed or removed by us, without the legal judgment of his peers" is the text's own if, and there was a legal judgment.
#ASSERT `ch 52 -- the lands, castles, franchises or right are to be restored` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Not obliged`
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30: was "#ASSERT `ch 52 -- the lands, castles, franchises or right are to be restored` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`"; now the text's no, because the same if, and he was not dispossessed or removed by the King.
#ASSERT `ch 52 -- the lands, castles, franchises or right are to be restored` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Not obliged`
-- expect: MUST `restore the lands, castles, franchises or right from which a man was dispossessed or removed without the legal judgment of his peers`
#TRACE `ch 52 -- we will immediately restore them to him` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 52 -- we will immediately restore them to him` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `restore the lands, castles, franchises or right from which a man was dispossessed or removed without the legal judgment of his peers` AT 6
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 52 -- we will immediately restore them to him` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- 52.2:
#ASSERT `ch 52 -- who decides a dispute over the restoration` TRUE EQUALS `the five-and-twenty barons`
#ASSERT `ch 52 -- who decides a dispute over the restoration` FALSE EQUALS `Forum not covered`
-- 52.3 and 52.4: arguments are taken without the lawful judgment of his peers by King Henry or King Richard, the King retains it or others to whom he is bound to warrant it possess it, a plea was raised or an inquest made before he took the cross, the usual term of crusaders has ended.
#ASSERT `ch 52 -- the King has respite for the possession` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS Entitled
#ASSERT `ch 52 -- the King has respite for the possession` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Not entitled`
#ASSERT `ch 52 -- the King has respite for the possession` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Not entitled`
#ASSERT `ch 52 -- the King has respite for the possession` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 52 -- the King has respite for the possession` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`
-- 52.5: the last argument is that the King has returned from his expedition or has desisted from it.
#ASSERT `ch 52 -- full justice is to be granted for the possession` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS Obliged
#ASSERT `ch 52 -- full justice is to be granted for the possession` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 52 -- full justice is to be granted for the possession` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 52 -- full justice is to be granted for the possession` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`
-- expect: MUST `grant full justice concerning the possessions for which he had respite`
#TRACE `ch 52 -- as soon as we return from our expedition we will immediately grant full justice therein` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 52 -- as soon as we return from our expedition we will immediately grant full justice therein` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `grant full justice concerning the possessions for which he had respite` AT 9
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 52 -- as soon as we return from our expedition we will immediately grant full justice therein` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
