#ASSERT `ch 56 -- who decides a dispute over the restoration to the Welshman` TRUE EQUALS `the judgment of the Welshman's peers in the marches`
#ASSERT `ch 56 -- who decides a dispute over the restoration to the Welshman` FALSE EQUALS `Forum not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 56 -- the law by which the dispute over a tenement is decided` `a tenement in England` EQUALS `the law of England`
#ASSERT `ch 56 -- the law by which the dispute over a tenement is decided` `a tenement in Wales` EQUALS `the law of Wales`
#ASSERT `ch 56 -- the law by which the dispute over a tenement is decided` `a tenement in the marches` EQUALS `the law of the marches`
#ASSERT `ch 56 -- the law by which the dispute over a tenement is decided` `a tenement elsewhere` EQUALS `Law not covered`
-- 56.4: arguments are he is a Welshman, he disseised or removed the King or his men, without the legal judgment of their peers.
#ASSERT `ch 56 -- the Welshman is to restore to the King and his men` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS Obliged
#ASSERT `ch 56 -- the Welshman is to restore to the King and his men` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 56 -- the Welshman is to restore to the King and his men` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`
